(a) Grounds for denial, revocation, or suspension of business occupation tax certificate. A business occupation tax certificate issued pursuant to any provision of this chapter may be denied, revoked or suspended at the discretion of the board of commissioners, or upon its authority by the county manager. More specifically, a business occupation tax certificate shall be denied, revoked, or suspended by the board of commissioners, or upon its authority by the county manager, and considered void, upon one or more of the following grounds:
(1) The original application or renewal thereof contains false or misleading information, the applicant omitted material facts in the application or the applicant has deliberately sought to falsify information contained therein;
(2) The premises covered by the certificate are found to be in violation of any county codes or ordinances;
(3) The applicant for, or holder of, the certificate is engaged in the business or occupation under a false or assumed name, or is impersonating another practitioner of a like or different name;
(4) The applicant for, or holder of, the certificate is engaging in false, misleading, or deceptive advertising or practices;
(5) The holder of the certificate is operating under a business or trade name not listed on the current application on file with the county;
(6) The holder of the certificate fails to maintain the initial requirements for obtaining the certificate;
(7) The applicant for, or holder of, a certificate is classified as, or becomes classified as, a habitual violator under title 40, chapter 5 of the Official Code of Georgia Annotated (O.C.G.A. § 40-5-58), or is found to be operating the business under the influence of alcohol or of illegal drugs or substances;
(8) The applicant for, or holder of, a certificate is addicted to the habitual use of intoxicating liquors, narcotics, or stimulants to such an extent the applicant or holder is unable to perform his duties under the business or occupation;
(9) The applicant for, or holder of, the certificate has been convicted of or has pled guilty or nolo contendere to any sexual offense, the offense of false swearing, the offense of operating an adult entertainment establishment in violation of the distance requirements of title 36, chapter 60 of the Official Code of Georgia Annotated (O.C.G.A. § 36-60-3), or to any offense involving the lottery, illegal possession or sale of narcotics or alcoholic beverages, or possession or receipt of stolen property, for a period of five years prior to the filing of the application. If after having been granted a certificate, the applicant is found to be not of good moral character, convicted, pleads guilty or enters a plea of nolo contendere to any of the offenses specified in this subsection, said certificate shall be subject to suspension and/or revocation;
(10) The applicant for, or holder of, the certificate fails to pay occupation taxes and administrative fees when due;
(11) The establishment has been declared a public or private nuisance or has created threat or nuisance to public health, safety or welfare;
(12) The applicant for, or holder of, the certificate is guilty of fraud in the operation of the business or occupation he practiced, or fraud or deceit in being licensed to practice in that area;
(13) Any other violation of this article; or
(14) Any violation of any rule or regulation of the county now in force or hereafter adopted.
(b) False or misleading information. No business tax certificate shall be issued or renewed pursuant to any provisions of this article to any applicant, business or legally or organizationally related entity if within the 12 months immediately preceding the filing with the department of finance of any application under this chapter the same applicant, business or legally or organizationally related entity has been denied a certificate or had a certificate revoked for any location based in whole or in part upon having furnished false or misleading information in any application or having omitted material facts in any application.
(c) No transfer of certificate. No business occupation certificate issued hereunder may be transferred.
(Ord. No. 2-2009, § 1(18-123), 2-2009)

